# Video: one factory, one check (Matt 2026-10-13)

Every video, from any bot (Cursor, Claude, Grok, Imagine) and on any machine, renders through this repo's `lib/studio` code. Imagine makes footage clips only, never a finished cut. Remotion is deleted, and the old box pipeline (`/workspace/motion-clips` HTML + `render.mjs`) is retired.

## The path

1. Read `.claude/skills/ryan-studio/SKILL.md` (the mandatory rules, the type cards, the brief schema, the technique menu) and `references/RULEBOOK.md` (Matt's locked rules, which win).
2. Write `brief.json` and `timeline.json`; `node .claude/skills/ryan-studio/tools/video_gate.mjs brief.json timeline.json` checks the paperwork.
3. `npm run studio:render -- brief.json timeline.json` renders the film and its manifest.
4. `npm run video:check -- final.mp4` measures the finished file. A separate reviewer signs off, then `npm run video:check -- final.mp4 --final` must pass. Only that goes to Matt. Matt posts himself.

Contract and every measured check: `docs/plans/STUDIO_ONE_FACTORY.md`. Craft: `.claude/skills/motion-design/SKILL.md`. Ad copy, voiceover markup and captions: `docs/ai-voiceover-scripts.md`.

## The spine (the same in every video, measured)

- Hook in the first 1 to 2 s, readable with the sound off.
- 15 to 30 s (a longer cut needs a written reason in the brief).
- Every beat holds at least 2.5 s; nothing on screen freezes.
- A warm female voiceover with TikTok-style captions timed from the final audio.
- One or two real numbers, each sourced (CLAUDE.md §0).
- Loops back into frame 0.
- Ends on the locked end card: logo, then Quality / Local / Service, then "Call now" 541.703.3095. A topic call to action gets its own card before it.
- Navy #102742 and cream #faf8f4; Amboqia for display words, Geist for numbers and captions; the logo only on the end card.
- Listing photos are moved at their true shape, never stretched, squeezed or regenerated.

## The creative layer (different every time)

Pick ready techniques from `.claude/skills/ryan-studio/techniques/registry.json`: at least one hook, one scene and one type technique. A planned technique is not built yet. A film whose hook device and scene set repeat any of the last five films fails the check.
